  a taught separation makes these NEGATIVE: the identity mapping asks the
  high-F1 posture for the LOW target and the swapped one asks it for the
  HIGH target.

  WHAT ALIGNMENT BUYS   aligned minus matched:  +1.0 +/- 0.3 Hz  (3.3 SE)
  the masking COST is held fixed across the two, so this is the part that
  is about the gesture rather than about confining credit at all.

  REVERSED, AND NOTHING PREDICTS IT. Aligning the block to the phase
  makes the mapping contrast +1.0 +/- 0.3 Hz MORE positive than the
  unaligned control (3.3 SE). A null and a reversal are different
  results and this is the second; it is reported and not explained.
